{"availability":"available","full":"gonzalo123/music-studio","name":"music-studio","description":"A browser-based guitar and keyboard practice studio, built as a pure vibe-coding experiment with React, TypeScript, Web MIDI and Tone.js.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-08T12:51:39Z","updated":"2026-08-08T12:56:16Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gonzalo123.github.io/music-studio/","topics":["ai-assisted-development","github-pages","guitar","keyboard","midi","music","music-education","piano","react","tone-js","typescript","vibe-coding","vite"],"demo":"https://gonzalo123.github.io/music-studio/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:11.712Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:11.712Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:11.712Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:11.712Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Not a DAW. Not a social network for musicians. Not another application that needs an account, a backend, a database and a subscription before it can play a C major chord.","The result is Music Studio: a React and TypeScript application with two instruments. The guitar module has scales, chords, guided practice, a tuner, a metronome, a harmony wheel and arpeggio exercises. The keyboard module can be played on screen or connected to a MIDI controller. It includes exercises, songs and a small four-bar jam studio.","Everything happens in the browser. There are no accounts and no backend. Preferences and a few local practice settings stay in localStorage."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gonzalo123/music-studio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d1542211de60bcffd2ef3de140aff27c94f72c8bb50daf457ecabda6cc59f7a2","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:11.798Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:11.798Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Not a DAW. Not a social network for musicians. Not anot